Author: Chen Xin
Date: JAN 05 2018
Version: V1.0.4

==========
SAS_Sim.py
==========
SAS_Sim.py is a python script which is used to simulate SAS server.
This simulator complies with part of SAS to CBSD Protocol TS V1.2

It supports following CBSD-SAS messages:
    registration
    spectrumInquiry
    grant
    heartbeat
    relinquishment
    deregistration

It also supports CBSD revocation and spectrum reassignment (suspend/terminate) 
by co-working with SAS Mananger.

You should configure the simulator before running it. You can open the configure
file -- SAS_Sim.conf via a text editor and change the default value of variables
if needed. 


==============
SAS_Manager.py
==============
SAS_Manager is a interactive tool which is alse writting in python. 
It can be used to show all information of CBSDs which are registed to SAS 
simulator. It also supports blacklist CBSD and suspend/terminate grant. 
You can run it and type help or ? to show all supported commands.


========================
!!!!! Restriction !!!!!!
========================
SAS_Sim and SAS_Manager are implemented by python and they have been tested
in python 2.7.3.  As we know, python3.x is incompatible with pyton2.x. So
you should check if python2.x is installed on your pc before you running 
SAS_Sim and SAS_Manager. If not, you can download python2.x from 
https://www.python.org/


==============
Change History 
==============
Version: V1.0.5
Updated to support TS1.2.

Version: V1.0.4
Added a config option -- tls_mutual_auth to control TLS mutual authentication.

Version: V1.0.3
Added support of response error code for specific sequence of message.

Version: V1.0.2
Added support of TLS mutual authentication.
Added support for spectrumInquiry with more than 10MHz frequency range.

Version: V1.0.1
Reduced sleep time to 1 day to avoid exception on Windows.
Added a config option -- enable_ipv6 to support IPv6 connection.

Version: V1.0.0
Aligned with TS1.1 without CPI support

Version: V0.3.2
Added a config option -- force_update_param/force_update_param_data to allow user 
to update any parameter with any value in response message
Added a config option -- reject_subsequent_connection to allow user to reject any 
incoming connection request after receiving a specified sas method request.
Added a config option -- force_http_response_code to allow user to set http 
response code in response message
Removed config option -- force_responseCode_invalid because we can use 
force_update_param/force_update_param_data instead.

Version: V0.3.1
Do not change CBSD/GRANT state if user configure force_response_code=0 &
force_exclude_param=<a valid value>. This change also apply to deregistration and 
relinquishment methods.

Version: V0.3.0
Do not change CBSD/GRANT state if user configure force_response_code=0 &
force_exclude_param=<a valid value>. This change only apply to following methods:
  registration
  grant
  heartbeat

Version: V0.2.9
Added a config option to allow user to remove a parameter from response message
Added a config option to allow user to set responseCode=999 in response message  

Version: V0.2.8
If a CBSD is blacklisted, set the transmitExpireTime to be a past time in
heartbeatResponse message.
Do not change the CBSD state if user use following options to specify the
responseCode = 101 (Blacklisted) in heartbeatResponse message
  force_sas_method = heartbeat
  force_response_code = 101

Version: V0.2.7
Reject grant request with responseCode = INTERFERENCE if the grant is still determined.
Removed options -- freeze_registrated_state & freeze_granted_state from config file.
Added a option -- blocked_request in config file to allow user to block any SAS request.
Added following options in config file to allow user to include a specified value of
responseCode in a response message. 
 - force_sas_method
 - force_response_code
 - force_response_data

Version: V0.2.6
After grant is terminated, still keep grant state until transmitExpireTime expire.
Fix a issue of relinquish.

Version: V0.2.5
Keep the transmitExpireTime included in HB response the same as the last HB
response even though the grant is terminated.

Version: V0.2.4
Reject the grant request with responseCode 400 if included freq is already existing 
on same CBSD.

Version: V0.2.3
Include transmitExpireTime in HeartbeatResponse message regardless of responseCode.

Version: V0.2.2
Respond registration with 105 (DEREGISTER) when receive duplicated register request. 
Update the field name heartbeatInterval instead of heartbeatDuration which is
included in GrantResponse.

Version: V0.2.1
Check operation state ignoring the case of the characters. 
Append \n\r to the data of http response message (Google SAS server uses
\n\r to indicate the end of http data).

Version: V0.2.0
Comply with TS1.0. Supported multiple Grants for one CBSD.

Version: V0.1.7
Supported 20MHz bandwidth.
If cmd 'transmit_renew' is disabled, do not extend transmit expire timer 
value even if first heartbeat request is received after timeout of transmit 
expire.

Version: V0.1.6
Fix issue that spectrum can not be assigned to more than one CBSDs.

Version: V0.1.5
Supported heartbeat/grant/transmit expire detection.

Version: V0.1.4
Added "grant_renew" cmd in SAS_Manager to enable/disable grant renewal.
Added "transmit_renew" cmd in SAS_Manager to enable/disable transmit renewal.
Changed the local time to UTC time which is inside grant response message or
heartbeat response message.
Changed the default log file to none to print logs through console.
Configured the tcp socket with blocking mode.

Version: V0.1.3
Added a feature to support configuration file. SAS_Sim will read this configure 
file in initialization phase. Please refer to "SAS_Sim.conf" for detailed 
information.

